import numpy as np

def feature(values, weights, remaining, capacity, taken):
    """If every candidate ends the build (leftover after each is below the min weight of the others), return value / max value; else zeros."""
    v = values.astype(np.float64)
    w = weights.astype(np.float64)
    k = v.shape[0]
    L = remaining - w
    if k == 1:
        m = np.array([np.inf])
    else:
        # all-pairs masked min: min over j != i of w[j]
        big = np.where(np.eye(k, dtype=bool), np.inf, w[None, :])
        m = big.min(axis=1)
    terminal = L < m
    if not np.all(terminal):
        return np.zeros(k)
    return v / max(v.max(), 1e-12)
```

This computes, only when every candidate's leftover (remaining − weight) is strictly below the smallest weight among the other candidates — i.e. taking any candidate ends the build — each candidate's value divided by the largest candidate value, and returns zeros otherwise; for k == 1 the "other candidates" minimum is taken as infinity so the single candidate is terminal.

